        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పరిపాలన",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పరిపాలన — paripālana — \"administration; governance\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మంచి పరిపాలన వల్ల జనం సంతోషంగా ఉన్నారు. mañci paripālana valla janaṁ santōṣaṅgā unnāru. Thanks to good administration the people are happy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From the same word as పాలించు, with పరి-, all round."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పరిపాలన (paripālana) is borrowed from Sanskrit paripālana, \"the act of guarding; fostering\" (Monier-Williams), pari-, \"all round\", added to pālana."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
